  "script": {
    "segments": [
      {
        "narration": "Sixty tonnes of iron fell here and left no crater. A plough hit it in 1920, on a farm outside Grootfontein, Namibia.",
        "visual_query": "namibian savanna farmland aerial",
        "visual_fallback": "african farmland"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Jacobus Brits heard metal screech under his blade. Underneath sat a slab nearly three metres across, eighty-four percent iron, sixteen percent nickel.",
        "visual_query": "rusted iron meteorite surface closeup",
        "visual_fallback": "iron surface"
      },
      {
        "narration": "So where is the crater? Something this heavy should have punched a hole visible from the air. The ground is flat.",
        "visual_query": "flat namibian desert scrubland",
        "visual_fallback": "desert scrub"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Its flat shape is the answer. The atmosphere braked it from over ten kilometres a second down to roughly two point seven.",
        "visual_query": "meteor streaking night sky",
        "visual_fallback": "night meteor"
      },
      {
        "narration": "It landed hard but not explosively, so it stayed whole. It fell under eighty thousand years ago and has never once been moved from the spot.",
        "visual_query": "grootfontein namibia dry bush landscape",
        "visual_fallback": "dry bushland"
      }
    ],
